        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "2e8ef1ae-1045-5625-bdbe-9c5b2d3b9d1f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Abraham Bankier, Oskar Schindler\n- Companies: Rekord factory\n- Places: Lipowa Street, Kraków, Poland, occupied Poland, Protectorate of Bohemia and Moravia\n- Roles: owner, industrialist, spy, Nazi Party member\n- Events: World War II, Holocaust\n\nFacts:\n- Abraham Bankier lived from 1910 to 1956.\n- Oskar Schindler lived from 28 April 1908 to 9 October 1974.\n- Abraham Bankier was one of the owners of the Rekord factory on Lipowa Street in Kraków, Poland.\n- During World War II, Oskar Schindler took over the Rekord factory on Lipowa Street in Kraków, Poland.\n- Oskar Schindler was a German industrialist, spy, and member of the Nazi Party.\n- During the Holocaust, Oskar Schindler is credited with saving the lives of 1,200 Jews by employing them in his enamelware and ammunitions factories.\n- Oskar Schindler’s factories were located in occupied Poland and the Protectorate of Bohemia and Moravia.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
